module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.AssociatedModule.Functor
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.Quasicoherent.Descent.Smallness
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.Etale.Precoverage
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.SmallEtaleEssentiallySmall
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.SmallEtaleStructureSheaf

/-!
# The associated-module functor of the small étale site of a scheme

Stacks Definition 03DU has four clauses.  Clause (1) is the structure sheaf of the big site
`(Sch/S)_τ` and clause (2) the structure sheaf of the small site `S_τ`; both are the sheaf of
rings `T/S ↦ Γ(T, 𝒪_T)`, and both are already established
(`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.structure_isSheaf` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.structure_isSheaf`).  Clause (3) is the sheaf of `𝒪`-modules
`𝓕 ↦ 𝓕^a`, `(f : T → S) ↦ Γ(T, f^*𝓕)`, on the big site, and is
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.baseAssociatedModule`.  **Clause (4) is the same functor on the
small site, and is what this module supplies for `τ = étale`.**

The construction is the one the big site uses: the inclusion of the small Zariski site of `S`
is continuous into the small étale site of `S`, the structure sheaves are compared over an open
`U` by identifying `Γ(𝒪_S, U)` with the global functions of the open subscheme `U`, and `𝓕^a`
is the pullback of sheaves of modules along the resulting morphism of ringed sites
`(S_étale, 𝒪) → (S_Zar, 𝒪_S)`.

What is étale-specific is the *continuity*, and it is harder here than on the big site.  There
the small Zariski site sits inside a slice category and `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver`'s
topology is a localization, so a covering sieve could be exhibited at the level of the ambient
category of schemes and then transported by `CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.mem_over_iff`.
The small étale site is *not* a localization of anything: it is a full subcategory cut out by
an object property, and its topology is generated by its own covering families, which carry a
cardinality bound.  The open covering cut out by a covering sieve of `S_Zar` has no such bound,
so it cannot be used as a witness directly.  The route taken instead descends the two full
inclusions `S_étale ⊆ (Sch/S)_étale ⊆ Sch_étale` using
`AlgebraicGeometry.smallEtale_precoverage_eq_comap` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.bigEtaleOver_precoverage_eq_comap`, settles the bound in the ambient category
with `AlgebraicGeometry.BigEtaleSite.exists_covering_rep`, and transports back along
`CategoryTheory.PreZeroHypercover.presieve₀_eq_of_combinatoriallyEquivalent`, combinatorially
equivalent families generating the same presieve.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigEtaleOver.opensToBigEtale`: the small Zariski site of `S` inside the big
  étale category over `S`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.opensToSmallEtale`: the small Zariski site of `S` inside the
  small étale site of `S`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.structureMap`: the comparison of structure sheaves, the ring
  half of the morphism of ringed sites `(S_étale, 𝒪) → (S_Zar, 𝒪_S)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.associatedModule`: **Stacks 03DU (4) at `τ = étale`**, the
  associated-module functor `𝓕 ↦ 𝓕^a`,
  `S.Modules ⥤ SheafOfModules (SmallEtale.structureSheaf B S hS)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.restrictModule`: its right adjoint, restriction along the
  inclusion of the small Zariski site.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.associatedModuleAdjunction`: the adjunction between them.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.presieve₀_mem_precoverage_of_isOpenImmersion`: a jointly
  surjective family of open immersions of the small étale site of `S` is a covering family.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.coverPreserving_opensToSmallEtale` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isContinuous_opensToSmallEtale`: the inclusion of the small
  Zariski site of `S` is cover preserving, hence continuous, into the small étale site.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.representablyFlat_opensToSmallEtale` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.final_opensToSmallEtale`: that inclusion is representably flat
  and final.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.hasWeakSheafify_smallEtale` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.wEqualsLocallyBijective_smallEtale`: abelian presheaves on the
  small étale site sheafify and the weak equivalences are the
  locally bijective maps.  These are what make the pullback of sheaves of modules exist.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.preservesColimitsOfSize_associatedModule`: the associated-module
  functor of the small étale site preserves all colimits.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isIso_pullbackObjUnitToUnit`: it takes the unit object to the
  unit object, the inclusion of the small Zariski site being final.

## Implementation notes

The clause string on `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.associatedModule` records exactly what is
proved.  Two things 03DU (4) is read with are *not* here.

First, the *sections formula*.  Clause (4) names `𝓕^a` by the formula
`(f : T → S) ↦ Γ(T, f^*𝓕)`, whereas the declaration here is the pullback along the morphism of
ringed sites; the two agree by Stacks 070S, whose big-site half is
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.baseAssociatedModuleIsoSections`.  Part (2) of 070S, the
corresponding statement for `S_étale`, *is* available — it is
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.sectionsComparisonSheafifiesToIso` in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Descent/AssociatedModule/SmallEtaleLocalBijectivity.lean`, proved
with no hypothesis — but that file is downstream of this one, so the identification cannot be
stated here and the clause string stays as it is.

Second, `τ = Zariski`.  Clause (4) is stated for `τ ∈ {Zariski, étale}`, and the Zariski half is
the same construction over `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallZariski`.  **That site does have a structure
sheaf in this library.**  It is `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallZariski.structureSheaf`
(`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Topologies/BigSites/SmallZariskiStructureSheaf.lean:85`), the
sheaf `T/S ↦ Γ(T, 𝒪_T)` of clause (2) at `τ = Zariski`, and it already carries
`add_to_stacks 03DU "small Zariski structure sheaf construction"`
(`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Topologies/SmallZariskiStructureSheaf.lean:32`); its sheaf
condition is proved from the equivalence `AlgebraicGeometry.smallZariskiSheafEquivWith` with
sheaves on the space of `S`, so it needs no fibre products in the site.  The wrong substitute —
reading `S_Zar` as `S.Opens` with `S.ringCatSheaf` and offering the identity functor — was
therefore never needed, and would indeed have stated something else, the coefficient sheaf of
clause (2) being isomorphic to `𝒪_S` and not equal to it.  What the Zariski half needed beyond
the structure sheaf was the comparison morphism of ringed sites `(S_Zar, 𝒪) → (S_Zar, 𝒪_S)` along
the inverse of `AlgebraicGeometry.smallZariskiSiteEquiv`, and that is now
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallZariski.structureMap`
(`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Descent/AssociatedModule/SmallZariskiRingedSite.lean:159`), with
the pullback along it
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallZariski.associatedModule` (`ibid.:180`), so clause (4) of the definition
is complete.

The structure-sheaf comparison is written out rather than taken from
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.structureMap`: the big-site comparison is a morphism into a
pushforward along `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.opensToBig`, a functor into a different
category, so there is no `rfl` between them even though both are
`CategoryTheory.forget₂`-of-`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Opens.topIso.inv` over each open.  The
naturality argument is the same, and is `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Opens.topIso_inv_appTop`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DU)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.BigEtaleOver

/-- An open subscheme of a scheme contained in a big étale site is contained in it. -/
public theorem contains_opens (B : BigEtaleSite.{u}) {S : Scheme.{u}} (hS : B.Contains S)
    (U : S.Opens) : B.Contains (U : Scheme.{u}) :=
  Scheme.size_lt_of_isOpenImmersion U.ι hS

variable (B : BigEtaleSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-- An open of `S` as an object of the big étale category over `S`, via its open immersion. -/
@[implicit_reducible]
public def opensObj (U : S.Opens) : BigEtaleOver B S hS :=
  Over.mk (ObjectProperty.homMk
    (X := B.obj (U : Scheme.{u}) (contains_opens B hS U)) U.ι)

/-- The structure morphism of `opensObj B S hS U` is the open immersion `U.ι`. -/
@[simp]
public theorem opensObj_hom_hom (U : S.Opens) :
    (opensObj B S hS U).hom.hom = U.ι := rfl

/-- The inclusion of one open of `S` into a larger one, as a morphism of the big étale
category over `S`. -/
@[implicit_reducible]
public noncomputable def opensHom {U V : S.Opens} (h : U ≤ V) :
    opensObj B S hS U ⟶ opensObj B S hS V :=
  Over.homMk (ObjectProperty.homMk
    (X := B.obj (U : Scheme.{u}) (contains_opens B hS U))
    (Y := B.obj (V : Scheme.{u}) (contains_opens B hS V)) (S.homOfLE h))
    (by
      apply ObjectProperty.hom_ext
      rw [ObjectProperty.FullSubcategory.comp_hom, opensObj_hom_hom, opensObj_hom_hom]
      exact S.homOfLE_ι h)

/-- The underlying morphism of schemes of `opensHom B S hS h` is `S.homOfLE h`. -/
@[simp]
public theorem opensHom_left_hom {U V : S.Opens} (h : U ≤ V) :
    (opensHom B S hS h).left.hom = S.homOfLE h := rfl

/-- The structure morphism of an object of the big étale category over `S` factors through the
open immersion of `U` whenever the object has a morphism to `U`. -/
public theorem hom_hom_eq {Z : BigEtaleOver B S hS} {U : S.Opens}
    (f : Z ⟶ opensObj B S hS U) : Z.hom.hom = f.left.hom ≫ U.ι := by
  rw [← opensObj_hom_hom B S hS U, ← ObjectProperty.FullSubcategory.comp_hom]
  exact congrArg (fun k : Z.left ⟶ B.obj S hS => k.hom) (Over.w f).symm

/-- The range of the structure morphism of an object of the big étale category over `S` lies in
an open `U` as soon as the object has a morphism to `U`. -/
public theorem range_le_of_hom {Z : BigEtaleOver B S hS} {U : S.Opens}
    (f : Z ⟶ opensObj B S hS U) : Set.range ⇑Z.hom.hom ⊆ (U : Set S) := by
  rw [← Scheme.Opens.range_ι U]
  rintro x ⟨y, rfl⟩
  exact ⟨f.left.hom y, by rw [hom_hom_eq B S hS f]; simp⟩

/-- An object of the big étale category over `S` whose structure morphism has range inside an
open `U` factors through `U`. -/
public noncomputable def homOfRangeLe {Z : BigEtaleOver B S hS} (U : S.Opens)
    (h : Set.range ⇑Z.hom.hom ⊆ (U : Set S)) : Z ⟶ opensObj B S hS U :=
  Over.homMk (ObjectProperty.homMk
      (IsOpenImmersion.lift U.ι Z.hom.hom (by rwa [Scheme.Opens.range_ι])))
    (by
      apply ObjectProperty.hom_ext
      rw [ObjectProperty.FullSubcategory.comp_hom, opensObj_hom_hom]
      exact IsOpenImmersion.lift_fac U.ι Z.hom.hom _)

/-- There is at most one morphism from an object of the big étale category over `S` to an open
of `S`, the open immersion of that open being a monomorphism. -/
public theorem subsingleton_hom_opensObj (Z : BigEtaleOver B S hS) (U : S.Opens) :
    Subsingleton (Z ⟶ opensObj B S hS U) := by
  refine ⟨fun f g => ?_⟩
  apply Over.OverMorphism.ext
  apply ObjectProperty.hom_ext
  rw [← cancel_mono U.ι, ← hom_hom_eq B S hS f, ← hom_hom_eq B S hS g]

/-- The small Zariski site of `S` inside the big étale category of schemes over `S`. -/
public noncomputable def opensToBigEtale : S.Opens ⥤ BigEtaleOver B S hS where
  obj U := opensObj B S hS U
  map {_ _} h := opensHom B S hS (leOfHom h)
  map_id U := by
    apply Over.OverMorphism.ext; apply ObjectProperty.hom_ext
    rw [opensHom_left_hom, Over.id_left, ObjectProperty.FullSubcategory.id_hom,
      Scheme.homOfLE_rfl]
    rfl
  map_comp f g := by
    apply Over.OverMorphism.ext; apply ObjectProperty.hom_ext
    rw [opensHom_left_hom, Over.comp_left, ObjectProperty.FullSubcategory.comp_hom,
      opensHom_left_hom, opensHom_left_hom, Scheme.homOfLE_homOfLE]

end AlgebraicGeometry.BigEtaleOver

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale

variable (B : BigEtaleSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-! ### The small Zariski site inside the small étale site -/

/-- An open of `S` is étale over `S`: its open immersion is étale. -/
public theorem isEtaleOver_opensObj (U : S.Opens) :
    BigEtaleOver.IsEtaleOver B S hS (BigEtaleOver.opensObj B S hS U) :=
  inferInstanceAs (Etale U.ι)

/-- An open of `S` as an object of the small étale site of `S`. -/
@[implicit_reducible]
public def opensObj (U : S.Opens) : SmallEtale B S hS :=
  ⟨BigEtaleOver.opensObj B S hS U, isEtaleOver_opensObj B S hS U⟩

/-- The small Zariski site of `S` inside the small étale site of `S`. -/
public noncomputable def opensToSmallEtale : S.Opens ⥤ SmallEtale B S hS where
  obj U := opensObj B S hS U
  map {_ _} h := ObjectProperty.homMk (BigEtaleOver.opensHom B S hS (leOfHom h))
  map_id U := ObjectProperty.hom_ext _ ((BigEtaleOver.opensToBigEtale B S hS).map_id U)
  map_comp f g := ObjectProperty.hom_ext _ ((BigEtaleOver.opensToBigEtale B S hS).map_comp f g)

/-- The underlying morphism of schemes of `(opensToSmallEtale B S hS).map h` is
`S.homOfLE (leOfHom h)`. -/
@[simp]
public theorem opensToSmallEtale_map_hom_left_hom {U V : S.Opens} (h : U ⟶ V) :
    ((opensToSmallEtale B S hS).map h).hom.left.hom = S.homOfLE (leOfHom h) := rfl

/-- Composing the inclusion of the small Zariski site of `S` into the small étale site with the
inclusion of the small étale site into the big étale site gives the inclusion of the small
Zariski site into the big étale site. -/
public theorem opensToSmallEtale_comp_inclusion :
    opensToSmallEtale B S hS ⋙ inclusion B S hS = BigEtaleOver.opensToBigEtale B S hS :=
  rfl

/-! ### Open coverings are small étale coverings -/

/-- **A jointly surjective family of open immersions of the small étale site of `S` is a
covering family.**  Such a family is an étale covering family of the ambient category of
schemes, so it has a combinatorially equivalent *selected* representative, and combinatorially
equivalent families generate the same presieve; the representative is then pulled back through
the two full inclusions `S_étale ⊆ (Sch/S)_étale ⊆ Sch_étale`. -/
public theorem presieve₀_mem_precoverage_of_isOpenImmersion {X : SmallEtale B S hS}
    (E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} X)
    (hsurj : ∀ x : ↥((toScheme B S hS).obj X),
      ∃ i, x ∈ Set.range ⇑((E.map (toScheme B S hS)).f i))
    (himm : ∀ i, IsOpenImmersion ((E.map (toScheme B S hS)).f i)) :
    E.presieve₀ ∈ precoverage B S hS X := by
  have hsmall : precoverage B S hS
      = (BigEtaleOver.precoverage B S hS).comap (inclusion B S hS) :=
    smallEtale_precoverage_eq_comap B (B.obj S hS)
  have hbig : BigEtaleOver.precoverage B S hS
      = B.precoverage.comap (Over.forget (B.obj S hS)) :=
    bigEtaleOver_precoverage_eq_comap B S hS
  rw [hsmall, Precoverage.mem_comap_iff, hbig, Precoverage.mem_comap_iff,
    ← PreZeroHypercover.presieve₀_map, ← PreZeroHypercover.presieve₀_map,
    BigEtaleSite.mem_precoverage_iff]
  have het : IsEtaleCovering (κ := B.cutoff)
      ⟨_, (E.map (inclusion B S hS)).map (Over.forget (B.obj S hS))⟩ :=
    (Scheme.presieve₀_mem_precoverage_iff _).mpr
      ⟨fun x => hsurj x, fun i => by
        have := himm i
        exact inferInstanceAs (Etale ((E.map (toScheme B S hS)).f i))⟩
  obtain ⟨W, hW, hcomb⟩ := B.exists_covering_rep _ het
  obtain ⟨W₀, F⟩ := W
  obtain ⟨hobj, hce⟩ := hcomb
  cases hobj
  dsimp only at hce
  exact ⟨F, PreZeroHypercover.presieve₀_eq_of_combinatoriallyEquivalent hce, hW⟩

/-- The covering family of the small étale site of `S` cut out by a covering sieve of the small
Zariski site of `S`: the open immersions of the members of the sieve. -/
public noncomputable def opensHypercover {U : S.Opens} (R : Sieve U) :
    PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} (opensObj B S hS U) where
  I₀ := ULift.{u + 1} (Σ V : S.Opens, { h : V ⟶ U // R.arrows h })
  X i := opensObj B S hS i.down.1
  f i := (opensToSmallEtale B S hS).map i.down.2.1

/-- A covering sieve of the small Zariski site of `S` cuts out a covering family of the small
étale site of `S`. -/
public theorem presieve₀_opensHypercover_mem_precoverage {U : S.Opens} (R : Sieve U)
    (hR : R ∈ Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥S U) :
    (opensHypercover B S hS R).presieve₀ ∈ precoverage B S hS (opensObj B S hS U) := by
  refine presieve₀_mem_precoverage_of_isOpenImmersion B S hS _ (fun x => ?_)
    (fun i => inferInstanceAs (IsOpenImmersion (S.homOfLE (leOfHom i.down.2.1))))
  obtain ⟨V, g, hg, hV⟩ := hR x.1 x.2
  refine ⟨⟨⟨V, g, hg⟩⟩, ⟨⟨x.1, hV⟩, ?_⟩⟩
  exact (Scheme.homOfLE_apply' (leOfHom g) x.1 hV).trans (Subtype.ext rfl)

/-- **The small Zariski site of `S` is cover preserving into the small étale site of `S`.**  An
open covering of an open `U` of `S` is a covering family of `U` in the small étale site, and the
sieve it generates refines the pushforward of the original covering sieve. -/
public theorem coverPreserving_opensToSmallEtale :
    CoverPreserving (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥S) (topology B S hS)
      (opensToSmallEtale B S hS) := by
  refine ⟨fun {U R} hR => ?_⟩
  refine (topology B S hS).superset_covering ?_
    (Precoverage.generate_mem_toGrothendieck
      (presieve₀_opensHypercover_mem_precoverage B S hS R hR))
  refine (Sieve.generate_le_iff _ _).2 ?_
  rintro Y g ⟨i⟩
  exact ⟨i.down.1, i.down.2.1, 𝟙 _, i.down.2.2, (Category.id_comp _).symm⟩

/-- An object of the small étale site of `S` whose structure morphism has range inside an open
`U` factors through `U`. -/
public noncomputable def homOfRangeLe {Z : SmallEtale B S hS} (U : S.Opens)
    (h : Set.range ⇑Z.obj.hom.hom ⊆ (U : Set S)) : Z ⟶ opensObj B S hS U :=
  ObjectProperty.homMk (BigEtaleOver.homOfRangeLe B S hS U h)

/-- There is at most one morphism from an object of the small étale site of `S` into the image
of an open of `S`, the open immersion of that open being a monomorphism. -/
public instance subsingleton_hom_opensToSmallEtale (Z : SmallEtale B S hS) (U : S.Opens) :
    Subsingleton (Z ⟶ (opensToSmallEtale B S hS).obj U) :=
  ⟨fun f g => ObjectProperty.hom_ext _
    ((BigEtaleOver.subsingleton_hom_opensObj B S hS Z.obj U).allEq f.hom g.hom)⟩

/-- **The small Zariski site of `S` is representably flat in the small étale site of `S`:** the
opens through which an object factors are closed under intersection and contain `⊤`, and the
factorization through each is unique. -/
public instance representablyFlat_opensToSmallEtale :
    RepresentablyFlat (opensToSmallEtale B S hS) := by
  refine ⟨fun Z => { cone_objs := ?_, cone_maps := ?_, nonempty := ?_ }⟩
  · intro A C
    have hA := BigEtaleOver.range_le_of_hom B S hS A.hom.hom
    have hC := BigEtaleOver.range_le_of_hom B S hS C.hom.hom
    exact ⟨StructuredArrow.mk (Y := A.right ⊓ C.right)
      (homOfRangeLe B S hS _ (Set.subset_inter hA hC)),
      StructuredArrow.homMk (homOfLE inf_le_left) (Subsingleton.elim _ _),
      StructuredArrow.homMk (homOfLE inf_le_right) (Subsingleton.elim _ _), trivial⟩
  · intro A C f g
    refine ⟨A, 𝟙 _, ?_⟩
    simp only [Category.id_comp]
    exact StructuredArrow.hom_ext f g (Subsingleton.elim _ _)
  · exact ⟨StructuredArrow.mk (Y := ⊤) (homOfRangeLe B S hS ⊤ (by simp))⟩

/-- The small Zariski site of `S` is a final subcategory of the small étale site of `S`: the
opens through which an object factors form a cofiltered, hence connected, category. -/
public instance final_opensToSmallEtale : (opensToSmallEtale B S hS).Final :=
  ⟨fun _ => IsCofiltered.isConnected _⟩

/-- The small Zariski site of `S` is continuous into the small étale site of `S`, so it induces
a morphism of sites `S_étale → S_Zar`. -/
public instance isContinuous_opensToSmallEtale :
    (opensToSmallEtale B S hS).IsContinuous (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥S)
      (topology B S hS) :=
  CategoryTheory.Functor.isContinuous_iff_coverPreserving.2
    (coverPreserving_opensToSmallEtale B S hS)

/-! ### Smallness and sheafification on the small étale site -/

/-- Abelian presheaves on the small étale site of `S` have a sheafification. -/
public instance hasWeakSheafify_smallEtale :
    HasWeakSheafify (topology B S hS) AddCommGrpCat.{u} := by
  have : HasSheafify (topology B S hS) AddCommGrpCat.{u} :=
    hasSheafifyEssentiallySmallSite.{u} _ _
  infer_instance

/-- Weak equivalences of abelian presheaves on the small étale site of `S` are the locally
bijective maps. -/
public instance wEqualsLocallyBijective_smallEtale :
    (topology B S hS).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u} :=
  GrothendieckTopology.WEqualsLocallyBijective.ofEssentiallySmall _

/-! ### The morphism of ringed sites and the associated-module functor -/

/-- The comparison of structure sheaves along the inclusion of the small Zariski site of `S`
into the small étale site of `S`: over an open `U` it is the identification of the sections of
`𝒪_S` over `U` with the global functions of the open subscheme `U`.  Together with the
continuity of the inclusion this is the morphism of ringed sites `(S_étale, 𝒪) → (S_Zar,
𝒪_S)`. -/
public noncomputable def structureMap :
    S.ringCatSheaf ⟶ ((opensToSmallEtale B S hS).sheafPushforwardContinuous RingCat.{u}
      (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥S) (topology B S hS)).obj (structureSheaf B S hS) where
  hom :=
    { app := fun U => (CategoryTheory.forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat.{u}).map
        (Scheme.Opens.topIso U.unop).inv
      naturality := fun U V h => by
        dsimp
        exact (((CategoryTheory.forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat.{u}).map_comp _ _).symm.trans
          ((congrArg _ (Scheme.Opens.topIso_inv_appTop (X := S) (leOfHom h.unop)).symm).trans
            ((CategoryTheory.forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat.{u}).map_comp _ _))) }

/-- The component of `structureMap B S hS` at an open `U` is the image in `RingCat` of the inverse
of `Scheme.Opens.topIso U.unop`. -/
@[simp]
public theorem structureMap_hom_app (U : (S.Opens)ᵒᵖ) :
    (structureMap B S hS).hom.app U
      = (CategoryTheory.forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat.{u}).map
          (Scheme.Opens.topIso U.unop).inv := rfl

/-- The pushforward of presheaves of modules along the structure-sheaf comparison of the small
étale site has a left adjoint. -/
public instance presheafPushforward_isRightAdjoint :
    (PresheafOfModules.pushforward.{u} (structureMap B S hS).hom).IsRightAdjoint :=
  Stacks.ModulePullback.isRightAdjoint_pushforward _

/-- The pushforward of sheaves of modules along the morphism of ringed sites of the small étale
site has a left adjoint. -/
public instance sheafPushforward_isRightAdjoint :
    (SheafOfModules.pushforward.{u} (structureMap B S hS)).IsRightAdjoint :=
  (SheafOfModules.PullbackConstruction.adjunction.{u} (structureMap B S hS)).isRightAdjoint

/-- **Stacks 03DU (4), at `τ = étale`.**  The associated-module functor of the small étale site
of `S`: the pullback of sheaves of modules along the morphism of ringed sites
`(S_étale, 𝒪) → (S_Zar, 𝒪_S)`. -/
@[stacks 03DU "associated module on the small site, clause (4) at τ = étale, functor only"]
public noncomputable def associatedModule :
    S.Modules ⥤ SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheaf B S hS) :=
  SheafOfModules.pullback.{u} (structureMap B S hS)

/-- Restriction of a sheaf of modules on the small étale site of `S` along the inclusion of the
small Zariski site of `S`, the right adjoint of the associated-module functor. -/
public noncomputable def restrictModule :
    SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheaf B S hS) ⥤ S.Modules :=
  SheafOfModules.pushforward.{u} (structureMap B S hS)

/-- The associated-module functor of the small étale site is left adjoint to restriction along
the inclusion of the small Zariski site. -/
public noncomputable def associatedModuleAdjunction :
    associatedModule B S hS ⊣ restrictModule B S hS :=
  SheafOfModules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction.{u} (structureMap B S hS)

/-- The associated-module functor of the small étale site is a left adjoint. -/
public instance isLeftAdjoint_associatedModule :
    (associatedModule B S hS).IsLeftAdjoint :=
  (associatedModuleAdjunction B S hS).isLeftAdjoint

/-- **Stacks 03DC, applied.**  The associated-module functor of the small étale site preserves
all colimits, being a left adjoint. -/
public noncomputable instance preservesColimitsOfSize_associatedModule.{w, w'} :
    PreservesColimitsOfSize.{w, w'} (associatedModule B S hS) :=
  (associatedModuleAdjunction B S hS).leftAdjoint_preservesColimits

/-- The pullback of the unit object along the morphism of ringed sites of the small étale site
is an isomorphism, the inclusion of the small Zariski site being final. -/
public instance isIso_pullbackObjUnitToUnit :
    IsIso (SheafOfModules.pullbackObjUnitToUnit.{u} (structureMap B S hS)) :=
  SheafOfModules.instIsIsoPullbackObjUnitToUnitOfFinal _

